## [v0.5.5.1 PARTNER ROSTER + PIVOT HOTFIX - 2026-07-24, UNCOMMITTED]
- Separated neutral source import from Player/Partner/NPC/Prop assignment.
  File drop and `+ Source` no longer force an NPC role; legacy explicit NPC and
  PROP import shortcuts remain available.
- Added four Resource Library role actions. The same source can back separate
  role profiles without changing its name, ID, path, or generic source kind.
  NPC/PROP roles create scene instances; Partner does not.
- Replaced the v0.5.5 Partner scene-actor interpretation with a
  `partner_profiles` standby roster. Removed Partner numbering/filtering,
  render/update/AI/physics, selection/focus, scene snapshots, HP, NPC count,
  and corpse paths. Resources exposes roster count and next candidate.
- Moved EX swap candidates and new swap role assignments to Partner. Partner
  swaps exchange PLAYER/PARTNER profile roles, rotate the outgoing profile
  back into the roster, and keep exact Player/NPC/PROP positions and NPC
  counts. Old NPC-based swaps remain a fallback for legacy data.
- Kept schema version 2 and added `partner` only as an optional existing
  profile-kind value. Kind-less legacy projects retain the old inference and
  are never force-migrated or saved. Legacy runtime `partner_list` actors are
  absorbed as roster profiles and then discarded as scene actors.
- Replaced fixed `player.y - 100` NPC spawning with a ground-coordinate spawn
  and stable profile ground offset. Explicit Aseprite pivot/anchor Slices win;
  otherwise the representative trimmed-frame bottom is aligned to ground.
- 109 targeted tests across 22 isolated modules passed. An initial broad
  example test invocation unintentionally reached one configured Aseprite
  integration case in a temporary directory; user JSON and source assets were
  not saved or modified. Full GUI/LAYERS integration, packaging, commits, and
  tags were not run. Protected user JSON, resources, build, and dist were not
  modified by this hotfix.

